      "text": "We need to evaluate the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\). To simplify this, we use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\).\n\nLet's break down the expression step-by-step and write the Python code to compute the result:\n\n1. Compute \\(19^2 - 17^2\\):\n\\[19^2 - 17^2 = (19 - 17)(19 + 17) = 2 \\cdot 36 = 72\\]\n\n2. Compute \\(15^2 - 13^2\\):\n\\[15^2 - 13^2 = (15 - 13)(15 + 13) = 2 \\cdot 28 = 56\\]\n\n3. Compute \\(11^2 - 9^2\\):\n\\[11^2 - 9^2 = (11 - 9)(11 + 9) = 2 \\cdot 20 = 40\\]\n\n4. Compute \\(7^2 - 5^2\\):\n\\[7^2 - 5^2 = (7 - 5)(7 + 5) = 2 \\cdot 12 = 24\\]\n\n5. Compute \\(3^2 - 1^2\\):\n\\[3^2 - 1^2 = (3 - 1)(3 + 1) = 2 \\cdot 4 = 8\\]\n\nNow, we sum all these results:\n\\[72 + 56 + 40 + 24 + 8\\]\n\nLet's compute the final sum using Python to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Calculate each term using the difference of squares formula\nterm1 = 19**2 - 17**2\nterm2 = 15**2 - 13**2\nterm3 = 11**2 - 9**2\nterm4 = 7**2 - 5**2\nterm5 = 3**2 - 1**2\n\n# Sum all the terms\nresult = term1 + term2 + term3 + term4 + term5\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n200\n```\nThe value of the expression \\(19^2 - 17^2 + 15^2 - 13^2 + 11^2 - 9^2 + 7^2 - 5^2 + 3^2 - 1^2\\) is \\(\\boxed{200}\\).",
